  "term": "hyoscine",
  "definition": "Hyoscine, also known as scopolamine, is a plant-derived tropane alkaloid from the nightshade family. It blocks acetylcholine activity at muscarinic receptors and has anticholinergic effects, including reducing nausea and vertigo and affecting secretions, pupil size, and gut movement.",
